<title>USA: Money Store gets 3-year $800 mln credit facility.</title>
<headline>Money Store gets 3-year $800 mln credit facility.</headline>
<dateline>UNION, N.J. 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money Store Inc said Monday it has secured a three-year $800 million, revolving credit facility.</p>
<p>The loan was arranged by a group of banks with First National Bank of Chicago and the First Union National Bank of North Carolina as lead banks, it said. The syndicate included 25 other lenders, it added.  </p>
<p>The new facility replaces Money Store's $400 million line. Borrowings under the new facility will be unsecured and proceeds will be used for general corporate purposes, it said.</p>
</text>
